@startuml outbound-projection
!include ../_includes/theme.puml

title Outbound projection with the guard and receipts

participant "Event journal\n(session host)" as J $COMMITTED
participant "Projections + DLP" as PROJ $SERVICE
participant "Outbound guard\n(optional, pinned model)" as GUARD $SERVICE
participant "Output consumer\n(app push, example)" as CONS $SERVICE
actor "Operator device" as DEV $PERSON
database "Audit hash chain" as AUD $COMMITTED

J -> PROJ : events at the audience-bound cursor

== Project and filter ==
PROJ -> PROJ : recheck audience and grants;\nrun deterministic DLP checks
alt audience revoked or no grant
  PROJ -> AUD : delivery_refused (no proposal exists;\nnothing flows further)
else audience admitted
  note right of PROJ
    Redaction creates a separately signed
    derivative referencing the source digests.
    Secret filters are best effort, never a
    substitute for audience authorization.
  end note
  PROJ -> AUD : proposal (digest, audience, policy)
  == Guard verdict ==
  alt guard disabled by declared configuration
    PROJ -> PROJ : proceed without a verdict\n(guardless configuration is explicit)
    == Deliver (guardless path) ==
    PROJ -> CONS : allowed proposal (exactly the checked bytes)
    CONS -> CONS : encrypt and sign\nfor the carrier
    CONS -> DEV : push wakes; app pulls state\nover an authenticated channel
    CONS -> AUD : transport evidence: enqueued / wake accepted\n(not an endpoint receipt)
    alt app fetches
      DEV -> CONS : fetch + endpoint-signed receipt\n(digest, recipient, status)
      CONS -> AUD : endpoint receipt (verified by the sender)
    else never fetched
      note right of CONS
        Transport evidence only: a wake the app
        never fetched is never reported as an
        endpoint receipt. Forged or mismatched
        receipts are rejected; a crash between
        send and receipt persistence reports
        unknown until evidence exists.
      end note
    end
  else guard enabled
    PROJ -> GUARD : verdict request (DLP-filtered immutable\nproposal content + classification context;\ndigest as the integrity binding)
    note right of GUARD
      The guard classifies content, not a bare
      digest — or a tightly scoped immutable
      reference whose resolution boundary is
      part of the approved design. The classifier
      endpoint is authorized as a data recipient
      before it sees private content.
    end note
    alt allow
      GUARD --> PROJ : allow
      == Deliver (allow path) ==
      PROJ -> CONS : allowed proposal (exactly the checked bytes)
      CONS -> CONS : encrypt and sign\nfor the carrier
      CONS -> DEV : push wakes; app pulls state\nover an authenticated channel
      CONS -> AUD : transport evidence: enqueued / wake accepted\n(not an endpoint receipt)
      alt app fetches
        DEV -> CONS : fetch + endpoint-signed receipt\n(digest, recipient, status)
        CONS -> AUD : endpoint receipt (verified by the sender)
      else never fetched
        note right of CONS
          Transport evidence only: a wake the app
          never fetched is never reported as an
          endpoint receipt. Forged or mismatched
          receipts are rejected; a crash between
          send and receipt persistence reports
          unknown until evidence exists.
        end note
      end
    else deny
      GUARD --> PROJ : deny
      PROJ -> AUD : guard_deny (no delivery follows)
    else review
      GUARD --> PROJ : review (pending, not delivered)
      PROJ -> DEV : release request (outside the agent's reach)
      DEV -> PROJ : exact-digest release or refusal
      alt released
        PROJ -> AUD : release (content, audience,\ndirection, policy)
        note right of PROJ
          Changing any of content, audience,
          direction or policy after review
          voids the release: renewed checks
          on the new identity are required.
        end note
        == Deliver (release path) ==
        PROJ -> CONS : allowed proposal (exactly the checked bytes)
        CONS -> CONS : encrypt and sign\nfor the carrier
        CONS -> DEV : push wakes; app pulls state\nover an authenticated channel
        CONS -> AUD : transport evidence: enqueued / wake accepted\n(not an endpoint receipt)
        alt app fetches
          DEV -> CONS : fetch + endpoint-signed receipt\n(digest, recipient, status)
          CONS -> AUD : endpoint receipt (verified by the sender)
        else never fetched
          note right of CONS
            Transport evidence only: a wake the app
            never fetched is never reported as an
            endpoint receipt. Forged or mismatched
            receipts are rejected; a crash between
            send and receipt persistence reports
            unknown until evidence exists.
          end note
        end
      else refused
        PROJ -> AUD : release_refused (no delivery follows)
      end
    else guard failure
      GUARD --> PROJ : timeout / provider error /\nmodel mismatch / malformed output
      PROJ -> AUD : guard_failure (fail-closed;\nno delivery follows)
    end
  end
end
note right of CONS
  Cursors and exports stay bound to
  audience and policy, rechecked at
  delivery. Revoked subscriptions close;
  delivered plaintext cannot be recalled.
  A summary cannot issue an approval.
end note

caption Sources: docs/architecture.md §5, §8, §12; docs/threat-model.md (mitigations, out of scope)
@enduml
